# word2ebook Maintenance Rules

## Source vs `wenda2_ebook/`

`wenda2_ebook/` is **generated output**. Never implement features by editing
files under `wenda2_ebook/` (HTML, concatenated `assets/js/script.js` /
`assets/css/style.css`, search indexes, etc.) — those are overwritten by
`python3 gen_all.py` / `main.py`.

Edit only under `tool/word2ebook/` (templates, `assets/js/modules/`,
`assets/css/modules/`, generators, `config.yaml`, specs), then rebuild so the
ebook is regenerated from source. See `tool/word2ebook/AGENTS.md` § Source vs
generated output.

## After Every Code Change

### 1. Update OpenSpec specs

When you modify behaviour in any Python module or JS/CSS module, update the
corresponding `openspec/specs/<domain>/spec.md`:

| Changed area | Spec to update |
|---|---|
| `main.py`, `Word2EBookConverter` | `overview/spec.md` |
| `core/document_parser.py` | `document-parsing/spec.md` |
| `generators/html_generator.py`, `generators/toc_generator.py`, `templates/` | `html-generation/spec.md` |
| `generators/search_generator.py`, `core/content_processor.py` | `search/spec.md` |
| `assets/js/modules/*.js` | `frontend-js/spec.md` |
| `assets/css/modules/*.css` | `frontend-css/spec.md` |
| `templates/static_assets.py` | `static-assets/spec.md` |
| `utils/i18n_utils.py`, `utils/config_utils.py`, `config.yaml` | `i18n/spec.md` |

### 2. Keep unit tests passing

Run the test suite after every change:

```bash
cd tool/word2ebook
python3 -m pytest tests/
```

- If you add a new function or class, add a corresponding test in `tests/test_<module>.py`
- If you change existing behaviour, update the affected test
- Target: maintain ≥ 80% coverage on all non-parser modules

### 3. JS/CSS module changes

The monolithic `script.js` and `style.css` have been **deleted**. The source of
truth is the module files:

- JS modules: `assets/js/modules/00-base.js` … `07-floating-controls.js`
  - Search split: `01b-search-index.js`, `01c-search-highlight.js`, `01d-search-perform.js`, `01e-search-ui.js`
  - Bookmarks split: `03a-bookmark-data.js`, `03b-bookmark-render.js`, `03c-bookmark-ui.js`
  - Reading settings: `03d-reading-settings.js`
- CSS modules: `assets/css/modules/00-base.css` … `05-responsive.css`
  - UX split: `01a-layout.css`, `01b-floating-toc.css`, `01c-bookmarks.css`
  - TOC split: `04a-toc-levels.css`, `04b-toc-dark.css`
  - All `@media` queries consolidated in `05-responsive.css`

`StaticAssetsManager` concatenates them automatically. Never re-create the
monolithic files — edit the appropriate module file instead.

**Key architectural rules:**
- CSS design tokens (`--color-primary`, `--radius-*`, `--shadow-*`) are defined in `00-base.css` `:root`; never use raw hex values in new CSS
- All `@media` rules belong in `05-responsive.css`; component files have no `@media` blocks
- Cross-module JS communication goes through the `W2E` namespace (`window.W2E`), not implicit globals
- Simplified/traditional HTML variants are generated by parameterised methods — never duplicate logic for the two language variants

### 4. Adding a new JS or CSS module

1. Create the file with the correct numeric prefix in `assets/{js,css}/modules/`
2. Verify `StaticAssetsManager.get_full_{js,css}_content()` picks it up
3. Add/update the `static-assets/spec.md` module table
4. Add a test in `tests/test_static_assets.py` confirming the new content appears in output
